const LEVELS=[
{"id":"beginner","kind":"level","order":1,"cls":"beg","name":"Beginner","years":"Year 0 – 1","tagline":"Clean messy data, build a star schema, write the core measures and ship one trustworthy page.","seo":"Beginner Power BI practice: clean data in Power Query, build a star schema, write core DAX measures and publish a report. Every assignment has a checkable result and a worked solution.","intro":"Everything here is done in Power BI Desktop with the mouse. If you can finish all five topics you are employable as a junior. Do not skip the date-table assignment: every later level assumes you did it.","topics":[{"id":"b-pq","name":"Getting data and cleaning it in Power Query","ds":["RawOrdersExport","DimProduct"],"skills":["power-query"],"stage":"analyst","refs":[{"title":"Power Query overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-query/power-query-what-is-power-query"},{"title":"Data profiling tools","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-query/data-profiling-tools"}],"asg":[{"t":"Turn the messy export into a clean table","time":"45 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport","guidance":"A","steps":["Load RawOrdersExport with Get Data → Enter Data.","Remove the first row (report header) and the last row (TOTAL) using Remove Top Rows and Remove Bottom Rows, not by filtering on a value.","Trim and Clean every text column. Rename headers to PascalCase with no spaces.","Fix Order Dt: use Column From Examples or Locale-aware Change Type so all seven date formats become one Date column. Check every row.","Strip $ and \" USD\" from Unit Price and convert to Decimal Number. Replace \"N/A\" with null, then convert Qty to Whole Number.","Capitalize Each Word on customer name and Region, so \"west \" and \"WEST\" both become \"West\".","Remove exact duplicate rows. Delete the fully empty LegacyFlag column."],"exp":"27 rows, 8 columns, no errors, no text-typed numbers. Qty column shows 3 nulls (two \"N/A\" values and one blank). Exactly 4 distinct Region values."},{"t":"Reproduce the same clean-up as a reusable query","time":"20 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport","guidance":"A","steps":["Right-click your cleaned query → Reference. Name it \"Orders Clean\".","In the original query, disable Enable Load so only the referenced query lands in the model.","Change one input value in the Enter Data source (e.g. change $199.99 to $209.99) and refresh: the clean query must update without a single manual step."],"exp":"Model contains one table, \"Orders Clean\". Query pane shows the raw query in italics (not loaded)."},{"t":"Join product attributes","time":"20 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport, DimProduct","guidance":"A","steps":["Load DimProduct.","In Orders Clean, Merge Queries with DimProduct on product name. Notice that \"TRAIL CHEF STOVE\" does not match: fix casing before the merge, not after.","Expand only Category and ProductKey.","Use Left Outer, then check the row count. Then try Inner and see which rows disappeared and why."],"exp":"All 27 rows keep a Category after the casing fix. The Inner join initially loses 1 row before the fix."},{"t":"Profile before you trust","time":"10 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport","guidance":"A","steps":["Turn on Column quality, Column distribution and Column profile in the View ribbon.","Change profiling from \"top 1000 rows\" to \"entire data set\".","Write down, for Qty: % valid, % error, % empty, distinct count, unique count."],"exp":"You can explain the difference between distinct and unique out loud (distinct = different values, unique = values that occur exactly once)."}],"int":[{"q":"What is the difference between Remove Duplicates and Remove Rows → Remove Errors, and when would each silently corrupt your data?","a":"Remove Duplicates only checks the selected columns, so selecting one column drops rows that differ elsewhere. Remove Errors removes the entire row, so a single unparseable date deletes a real sale. Fix the type conversion (locale, Replace Values) so errors don't occur, and only remove errors as a last resort you can justify."},{"q":"Why does Change Type to Date fail on \"Jan 7 2026\" and \"06/02/2026\" in the same column, and how do you fix it?","a":"Type detection uses one culture. Use Change Type with Locale for a consistent format, or Column From Examples to build a parsing step. For truly mixed formats, split into a conditional column that tries Date.FromText with different cultures via try…otherwise."},{"q":"Someone applied steps in the wrong order: Change Type before Replace Values. What breaks?","a":"The type step errors on \"$199.99\" before replace runs. Steps are a pipeline; drag Replace Values above Change Type, or delete the auto-detected Changed Type step and re-add it at the end."},{"q":"What is query folding and how can a beginner check whether a step folds?","a":"Folding pushes the transformation back to the source as SQL. Right-click a step → View Native Query. If it is greyed out, folding stopped at or before that step. Enter Data never folds because there is no source engine."},{"q":"When is a Reference better than a Duplicate?","a":"Reference keeps a live link so the cleaning logic exists once. Duplicate copies the steps and they drift apart. Use Reference for staging → clean → model layers, Duplicate when you intentionally want two independent queries."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"After Remove Top Rows(1) and Remove Bottom Rows(1) on RawOrdersExport, how many rows remain before de-duplication?","o":["27","28","29","30"],"a":1,"why":"30 total minus the header row and the TOTAL row = 28. Removing the one duplicate SO-5001 line gets you to 27."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which step turns \"$699.99\" into a usable number with the fewest chances of error?","o":["Change Type → Decimal Number directly","Replace \"$\" with \"\" then Change Type","Split column by delimiter \"$\"","Extract text after delimiter"],"a":1,"why":"Replace then type-convert is explicit and survives future values like \"$1,299.00\" after you also replace commas."},{"type":"task","q":"Load RawOrdersExport and produce a table with exactly these column types: OrderRef Text, OrderDate Date, CustomerName Text, Product Text, Qty Whole Number, UnitPrice Decimal, Region Text, Notes Text. Zero error cells. Screenshot the Applied Steps pane.","hint":"Order of steps: remove rows → replace values → trim/clean/capitalize → change type → remove duplicates."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Column profile says Qty has distinct = 9 and unique = 3. What does unique = 3 mean?","o":["3 rows have Qty","3 different values of Qty appear only once","3 nulls","3 errors"],"a":1,"why":"Unique counts values that occur exactly one time; distinct counts different values."}],"module":"beginner"},{"id":"b-model","name":"Data modeling: a star schema that behaves","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct","DimCustomer","DimRegion","DimDate"],"skills":["modeling"],"stage":"analyst","refs":[{"title":"Star schema guidance for Power BI","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/guidance/star-schema"},{"title":"Create date tables","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/guidance/model-date-tables"}],"asg":[{"t":"Build the Northwind star","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSales + 4 dims","guidance":"A","steps":["Load FactSales, DimProduct, DimCustomer, DimRegion and DimDate.","In Model view, delete every auto-detected relationship. Rebuild them yourself: DimProduct[ProductKey] → FactSales[ProductKey], same for Customer, Region and DimDate[Date] → FactSales[OrderDate].","Set every relationship to One-to-Many, single direction, filter flowing from dimension to fact.","Mark DimDate as a date table.","Hide every key column in the fact table from Report view."],"exp":"Four relationships, all 1:*, all single-direction arrows pointing at FactSales. Card visual showing COUNTROWS(FactSales) = 100."},{"t":"Replace DimDate with a DAX date table","time":"20 min","ds":"DimDate","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a new table: Dates = CALENDAR(DATE(2025,1,1), DATE(2026,12,31)).","Add columns Year, MonthNumber, MonthName, YearMonth (as \"2026-03\"), Quarter, IsWeekend.","Sort MonthName by MonthNumber. Mark as date table. Relate to FactSales[OrderDate]. Delete the loaded DimDate.","Build a column chart of FactSales quantity by MonthName: months must appear Jan, Feb, Mar (not alphabetically)."],"exp":"730 rows in Dates. Chart order Jan → Feb → Mar. Note: the loaded DimDate stops at 31 Mar 2026, which is exactly why you replaced it."},{"t":"Find the join that lies","time":"20 min","ds":"FactSales, DimCustomer, DimRegion","guidance":"A","steps":["Notice that both FactSales and DimCustomer contain a RegionKey.","Create two relationships from DimRegion: one to FactSales[RegionKey], one to DimCustomer[RegionKey]. Power BI will make one of them inactive (dashed line).","Build a table: RegionName, Sum of Quantity. Change which relationship is active and compare.","Decide which is correct for \"sales by region where the sale happened\" versus \"sales by region of the customer's home\". Keep the one to FactSales active."],"exp":"Region totals change, but the grand total (333 units) does not: 79 of the 100 sales lines were sold by a rep whose region is not the customer's home region."},{"t":"Role-playing date","time":"15 min","ds":"FactSales, Dates","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a second relationship Dates[Date] → FactSales[ShipDate]. It will be inactive.","Write: Shipped Qty = CALCULATE(SUM(FactSales[Quantity]), USERELATIONSHIP(Dates[Date], FactSales[ShipDate])).","Matrix by MonthName with Sum of Quantity and Shipped Qty side by side."],"exp":"March shows more ordered than shipped because some late-March orders ship in April, outside the fact range."}],"int":[{"q":"Why single-direction relationships by default? Give one concrete bug bi-directional filtering causes.","a":"Bi-directional filters create ambiguity and cost performance. Concrete bug: with DimCustomer ↔ FactSales both ways, a slicer on Product filters the customer list to only customers who bought that product, which looks helpful but makes every other slicer behave unpredictably and breaks RLS propagation."},{"q":"What makes a table a \"proper\" date table and what breaks if it is not one?","a":"Contiguous dates, one row per day, covering the full range of every fact, a unique date column, marked as date table. Without it, time-intelligence functions like DATEADD and TOTALYTD return wrong results or blanks, and auto date/time hidden tables bloat the model."},{"q":"Explain snowflake vs star and why Power BI prefers star.","a":"Snowflake normalises dimensions (Product → SubCategory → Category tables). Star flattens them into one table. VertiPaq compresses repeated text well, so flattening costs little, and every extra hop is an extra relationship the engine must traverse per query."},{"q":"You have a fact table with 100 rows and a Product dimension with 24 rows, but the visual total does not match the fact table sum. Name three causes.","a":"(1) a ProductKey in the fact with no match in the dimension (blank row absorbing them), (2) a duplicate key in the dimension turning the relationship into many-to-many, (3) an inactive or wrong-direction relationship."},{"q":"When do you actually want a calculated column instead of a measure?","a":"When the value is needed on an axis, slicer or as a relationship key, or for row-level categorisation (e.g. \"Order size bucket\"). Everything aggregated should be a measure. Calculated columns are computed at refresh and stored, so they cost memory."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"FactSales has a ProductKey of 25 that does not exist in DimProduct. What does a table of Category by Quantity show?","o":["An error","The row is dropped","A row with blank Category holding that quantity","The quantity spreads across all categories"],"a":2,"why":"Referential integrity violations are collected into an invisible blank member of the dimension."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which relationship must be inactive?","o":["DimRegion → FactSales","Dates → FactSales[OrderDate]","Dates → FactSales[ShipDate]","DimProduct → FactSales"],"a":2,"why":"Two relationships between the same pair of tables cannot both be active; you activate ShipDate on demand with USERELATIONSHIP."},{"type":"task","q":"Build the star and produce a matrix: rows = Category, columns = RegionName, values = Sum Quantity. Report the value for Water × West.","hint":"If your value is 0 or blank, check the direction of the Region relationship."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Marking a table as a date table requires:","o":["A column of type Date/Time","A unique Date column with no nulls and no gaps","At least 365 rows","A column named \"Date\""],"a":1,"why":"Uniqueness and contiguity are validated; the name and row count are not."}],"module":"beginner"},{"id":"b-dax","name":"DAX fundamentals: measures that add up","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct","DimCustomer"],"skills":["dax"],"stage":"analyst","refs":[{"title":"DAX basics in Power BI Desktop","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/desktop-quickstart-learn-dax-basics"},{"title":"DAX function reference","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/dax-function-reference"}],"asg":[{"t":"The core measure set","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSales, DimProduct","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a dedicated \"_Measures\" table (Enter Data, one dummy column, delete it after the first measure).","Write: Total Qty, Gross Sales = SUMX(FactSales, FactSales[Quantity] * FactSales[UnitPrice]), Discount Amt = SUMX(FactSales, FactSales[Quantity] * FactSales[UnitPrice] * FactSales[Discount]), Net Sales = [Gross Sales] - [Discount Amt].","Write COGS = SUMX(FactSales, FactSales[Quantity] * RELATED(DimProduct[UnitCost])) and Margin % = DIVIDE([Net Sales] - [COGS], [Net Sales]).","Format every currency measure as $ with 2 decimals, Margin % as percentage with 1 decimal."],"exp":"A card for Net Sales shows a positive number. Margin % between 40% and 65% at the total level. Returns (negative quantity) reduce the totals automatically."},{"t":"Counting things correctly","time":"20 min","ds":"FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Write Order Lines = COUNTROWS(FactSales), Orders = DISTINCTCOUNT(FactSales[OrderID]), Customers Buying = DISTINCTCOUNT(FactSales[CustomerKey]).","Write Avg Order Value = DIVIDE([Net Sales], [Orders]).","Put all four in a table by Channel, then by Category. In both, check whether the Orders total equals the sum of the rows. Channel is stored on each line here, so one order can span channels as well as categories."],"exp":"Order Lines total = 100. Orders total = 54. Orders by Channel adds up to 77 and Orders by Category to 89, both more than 54, because one order can span channels and categories. A distinct count never adds up across rows."},{"t":"First CALCULATE","time":"25 min","ds":"FactSales, DimProduct","guidance":"A","steps":["Write Camping Sales = CALCULATE([Net Sales], DimProduct[Category] = \"Camping\").","Put it in a table by Category. Observe the same number on every row. Explain why to yourself before continuing.","Write Sales All Categories = CALCULATE([Net Sales], REMOVEFILTERS(DimProduct[Category])) and % of Total = DIVIDE([Net Sales], [Sales All Categories]).","Add a Region slicer. % of Total must still sum to 100% within the selected region."],"exp":"% of Total column sums to exactly 100% with or without a region selected."},{"t":"Calculated columns you can defend","time":"15 min","ds":"FactSales, DimCustomer","guidance":"A","steps":["On FactSales add Line Type = IF(FactSales[Quantity] < 0, \"Return\", \"Sale\").","On DimCustomer add Tenure Years = DATEDIFF(DimCustomer[JoinDate], DATE(2026,3,31), YEAR).","On DimCustomer add Tenure Band = SWITCH(TRUE(), [Tenure Years] >= 3, \"3+ yrs\", [Tenure Years] >= 1, \"1–2 yrs\", \"New\").","Use Line Type as a slicer and Tenure Band on an axis. Now explain why neither could have been a measure."],"exp":"Slicer shows Sale / Return. Return count is 7."}],"int":[{"q":"Why SUMX(FactSales, Quantity * UnitPrice) rather than a calculated column Amount then SUM?","a":"The column stores 100 extra values (millions in real life) that compress poorly because they are nearly unique. SUMX computes on the fly and is usually just as fast for simple arithmetic. Rule: store what you slice by, compute what you sum."},{"q":"What does DIVIDE do that / does not?","a":"Returns BLANK (or an alternate result) on division by zero instead of an error, and BLANK rows disappear from visuals, which is usually what you want."},{"q":"Explain \"filter context\" with the Camping Sales example.","a":"Every cell in a visual is evaluated with filters coming from rows, columns, slicers and page filters. CALCULATE with Category = \"Camping\" overwrites the Category filter, so every row shows the Camping number regardless of the row's category."},{"q":"Why do DISTINCTCOUNT totals not add up across rows?","a":"The same OrderID can appear under several categories; the total counts it once, the rows count it once each. Non-additive measures are correct by design; teach your users, do not \"fix\" the total."},{"q":"What is the difference between BLANK and 0 in a visual, and how do you show 0?","a":"Blank rows are removed from visuals; zeros are shown. To force zeros use [Measure] + 0 (careful, it will show every dimension member) or the \"Show items with no data\" option."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"CALCULATE([Net Sales], DimProduct[Category] = \"Camping\") in a table by Category shows:","o":["Camping sales only on the Camping row","The Camping number on every row","An error","Blank on non-Camping rows"],"a":1,"why":"The filter argument replaces the existing Category filter on every row."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which is correct for average price per unit sold?","o":["AVERAGE(FactSales[UnitPrice])","DIVIDE([Gross Sales], [Total Qty])","AVERAGEX(FactSales, FactSales[UnitPrice])","SUM(UnitPrice) / COUNTROWS(FactSales)"],"a":1,"why":"A weighted average must divide total revenue by total units; the others average line prices regardless of quantity."},{"type":"task","q":"Build a table: Segment, Net Sales, Margin %, Orders, Avg Order Value. Which Segment has the highest Avg Order Value? State the value.","hint":"Outfitter buys in larger quantities; check your DISTINCTCOUNT is on OrderID not SalesKey."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Tenure Band should be a calculated column because:","o":["Measures cannot use SWITCH","It must be usable on an axis and slicer","It is faster","Columns can reference other columns"],"a":1,"why":"Axes and slicers need stored values; measures only exist inside visual cells."}],"module":"beginner"},{"id":"b-viz","name":"Visualisation and report design","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct","DimCustomer","DimRegion"],"skills":["visuals","communication"],"stage":"analyst","refs":[{"title":"Tips for designing a great report","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-tips-and-tricks-for-creating-reports"},{"title":"Conditional formatting in tables","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-conditional-table-formatting"}],"asg":[{"t":"The one-page executive summary","time":"45 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Page size 16:9. Add a title, four cards (Net Sales, Orders, Margin %, Customers Buying), a column chart Net Sales by MonthName, a bar chart Net Sales by Category sorted descending, a map or filled map by State, and a slicer for RegionName.","Use one accent colour for the \"good\" series and grey for everything else. No more than two font sizes besides the title.","Enable \"Edit interactions\" and make the category bar chart cross-highlight the month chart but not filter the cards.","Add a page-level filter Line Type = Sale, and a card that shows Return count using CALCULATE with REMOVEFILTERS on that column."],"exp":"A colleague can answer \"which region is behind?\" within 5 seconds of looking at the page."},{"t":"Conditional formatting that means something","time":"20 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Table: ProductName, Net Sales, Margin %.","Margin %: background colour rules → red below 40%, amber 40–55%, green above 55%.","Net Sales: data bars.","Add an icon set on Margin % using the same thresholds. Then remove the data bars: a table with three formats is noise."],"exp":"Discontinued products cluster in the red/amber bands."},{"t":"Slicer behaviour","time":"15 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Add a Category slicer (list), a Date slicer (between), a LoyaltyTier slicer (dropdown, multi-select with Ctrl off).","Sync the Category slicer to a second page via View → Sync slicers.","Add a \"Clear all slicers\" button using a bookmark with slicers reset."],"exp":"Changing Category on page 1 changes page 2; clicking the button resets both."},{"t":"Matrix mastery","time":"20 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Matrix rows: Category → SubCategory, columns: MonthName, values: Net Sales.","Turn on stepped layout off, subtotals per level, expand all one level down.","Add Margin % as a second value and switch \"Show on rows\" so values stack vertically.","Apply conditional formatting to only Net Sales, not to subtotals (there is a toggle)."],"exp":"Matrix reads like a financial statement, not a spreadsheet dump."}],"int":[{"q":"When is a pie chart acceptable?","a":"Two to three parts of one whole, when the message is \"A is roughly half\". Anything else is a bar chart. Donuts add nothing except space for a number."},{"q":"What is the difference between cross-filter and cross-highlight?","a":"Cross-highlight keeps all bars and dims the unselected part; cross-filter removes unselected data entirely. Highlight is better for \"share of\", filter for \"drill into\"."},{"q":"How do you make a report load faster from the visual side alone?","a":"Fewer visuals per page (each is at least one query), no slicers with thousands of values, avoid tables with 20 columns of measures, turn off unnecessary interactions, use a Top N filter instead of showing every product."},{"q":"Why should you avoid implicit measures (dragging a numeric column onto a visual)?","a":"The aggregation is decided per visual and can silently be wrong (Sum of UnitPrice), you cannot reference it from other measures, and it breaks with calculation groups."},{"q":"A stakeholder asks for a \"dashboard\". What do you ask before you build?","a":"Who looks at it, how often, which decision does it drive, which single number matters most, and what is the definition of that number (net or gross, returns included or not). Then confirm the definition in writing."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"You want the total row of a table to show \"Total\" instead of blank in the first column. Where?","o":["Format the column","Format visual → Totals → Row label","Write a measure","Not possible"],"a":1,"why":"Totals settings include a row label option."},{"type":"mcq","q":"A visual shows 24 products but the stakeholder wants the top 5 by Net Sales. Best approach:","o":["Sort descending and hope","Visual-level filter Top N on ProductName by Net Sales","Calculated column IsTop5","Filter the query in Power Query"],"a":1,"why":"Top N is dynamic and respects other filters."},{"type":"task","q":"Build the executive summary page. Add a Bookmark called \"Water only\" that pre-selects Category = Water and shows a hidden text box saying \"Water category view\". Attach it to a button.","hint":"Bookmark must be set with Data on and the Selection pane used to hide the text box in the default state."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which visual best shows Net Sales this month versus last month for 4 regions?","o":["Pie","Clustered bar","Stacked bar","Gauge"],"a":1,"why":"Clustered bars allow direct comparison of two values per category."}],"module":"beginner"},{"id":"b-service","name":"Power BI Service basics","ds":["FactSales"],"skills":["service"],"stage":"analyst","verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Power BI service sharing, apps and refresh docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Ways to share your work","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/collaborate-share/service-share-dashboards"},{"title":"Publish an app","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/collaborate-share/service-create-distribute-apps"},{"title":"Configure scheduled refresh","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/refresh-scheduled-refresh"}],"asg":[{"t":"Publish and share properly","time":"25 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a workspace \"Northwind Dev\". Publish the report.","Open the semantic model settings. Note that Enter Data sources cannot be refreshed and that this is fine for now.","Share the report with a colleague (or a second account) with \"Allow recipients to share\" off and \"Build\" permission off.","Have them open it. Confirm they cannot see the workspace itself."],"exp":"The colleague sees only the report, not the model or workspace."},{"t":"App versus share","time":"20 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Create an App from the workspace with the report inside. Add an audience.","Compare what the consumer sees via the App link versus via direct share.","Update the report, republish, and update the App. Note that until you update the App, consumers see the old version."],"exp":"You can explain when a change is visible to App users and when it is not."},{"t":"Dashboard versus report","time":"15 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Pin the four cards to a new dashboard \"Northwind KPI\".","Set a data alert on the Net Sales tile.","Try to add a slicer to the dashboard. Notice that you cannot."],"exp":"You can state two things a dashboard does that a report cannot (alerts, tiles from multiple reports) and two things it cannot do (slicers, interactions)."},{"t":"Refresh that actually works","time":"20 min","ds":"Any CSV on OneDrive","guidance":"A","steps":["Save one of the datasets as CSV in OneDrive for Business. Point a new report at it via Get Data → Web using the OneDrive share link ending in ?download=1, or via the SharePoint folder connector.","Publish. Set credentials on the semantic model (OAuth). Schedule refresh daily at 6:00 in your timezone.","Edit the CSV, wait for or trigger a refresh, confirm the report changed."],"exp":"Refresh history shows Completed. The edited value appears in the Service without republishing."}],"int":[{"q":"What is the difference between a report, a semantic model, a dashboard and an app?","a":"Semantic model = the data and measures; report = pages of visuals on top of one model; dashboard = single canvas of pinned tiles from one or more reports, no slicers; app = packaged, read-only distribution of workspace content with its own navigation and audiences."},{"q":"A viewer says \"I can't see the report\". Walk through your checklist.","a":"License (Pro/PPU or Fabric capacity), permission on the report, permission on the underlying model if it lives in another workspace, RLS role membership, App audience membership, whether they opened the App link or the workspace link."},{"q":"Why does a scheduled refresh fail for a file on your desktop?","a":"The Service cannot reach your machine. Either move the file to OneDrive/SharePoint or install an on-premises data gateway (personal mode is fine for one user, standard mode for teams)."},{"q":"What does Build permission allow?","a":"Creating new reports on the shared semantic model (in the Service, Desktop live connect, Excel Analyze). Read permission only lets someone view existing reports."},{"q":"What are the workspace roles and which one would you never give a business user?","a":"Viewer, Contributor, Member, Admin. Never Admin (can delete the workspace) and rarely Member (can share and publish apps)."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"You republish a report from Desktop. Which is true?","o":["App users see changes instantly","Direct-share users see changes instantly, App users after App update","Nobody sees changes until refresh","Both see changes after refresh"],"a":1,"why":"Apps are a published snapshot of the workspace content."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Data alerts can be set on:","o":["Any visual in a report","Cards, KPIs and gauges pinned to a dashboard","Slicers","Matrix cells"],"a":1,"why":"Alerts are a dashboard feature for single-value tiles."},{"type":"task","q":"Configure scheduled refresh for a OneDrive CSV, force a failure by renaming the file, read the error message, fix it, and write down the exact error text you saw.","hint":"The error mentions the path or 404; knowing what it looks like saves you 30 minutes in production."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Minimum requirement for a colleague to view a report in a Pro workspace:","o":["Nothing","A free account","A Pro or PPU license","Fabric admin"],"a":2,"why":"Pro workspaces require Pro/PPU for consumers; free users can only consume from capacity-backed workspaces."}],"module":"beginner"}]},
{"id":"intermediate","kind":"level","order":2,"cls":"int","name":"Intermediate","years":"Year 1 – 3","tagline":"Filter context, time intelligence, row-level security, gateways and the Service.","seo":"Intermediate Power BI practice: M functions, many-to-many models, CALCULATE and filter context, time intelligence, RLS and refresh. Assignments with checkable results and worked solutions.","intro":"Now you write M and DAX by hand and you start using DAX Studio and Tabular Editor. The goal of this level is that filter context stops being magic. Every measure you write here should be one you can explain line by line.","topics":[{"id":"i-pq","name":"Advanced Power Query and M","ds":["SurveyWide","RawOrdersExport","ExchangeRates","FactSales"],"skills":["power-query"],"stage":"developer","refs":[{"title":"Power Query M function reference","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powerquery-m/power-query-m-function-reference"},{"title":"Query folding guidance","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-query/query-folding-basics"}],"asg":[{"t":"Unpivot the wide survey","time":"20 min","ds":"SurveyWide","guidance":"A","steps":["Load SurveyWide. Select StoreCode, StoreName, RegionKey → Unpivot Other Columns.","Split Attribute on \"-\" into Month and Year. Build a real date (first of month) from them.","Move Target-2026 into its own query (it is not a month) before unpivoting, then merge it back as a column.","Open Advanced Editor and read the generated M top to bottom. Rename every step so the pipeline reads like a sentence."],"exp":"36 rows (12 stores × 3 months) with a MonthDate column and a Target column repeated per row."},{"t":"Write a custom function","time":"30 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a blank query with this function: (t as text) as nullable number => let s = Text.Remove(t, {\"$\",\" \",\"U\",\"S\",\"D\"}), n = try Number.From(s) otherwise null in n","Name it fnCleanMoney. Invoke it on Unit Price via Add Column → Invoke Custom Function.","Write a second function fnParseDate that tries three cultures in order: \"en-US\", \"en-GB\", then Date.FromText with no culture.","Apply it to Order Dt and verify every row."],"exp":"Zero errors; \"N/A\" becomes null; \"09-01-2026\" becomes 9 Jan 2026 or 1 Sep 2026, and you can state which and why (order of cultures tried)."},{"t":"Parameters and a switchable environment","time":"20 min","ds":"Any","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a text parameter Environment with values Dev, Test, Prod.","Create a query Config with a table mapping Environment → source path (use three copies of a CSV in three OneDrive folders).","Make the main source step read the path from Config via a lookup on the parameter.","Switch the parameter and refresh. Then publish and change the parameter in the Service (Settings → Parameters)."],"exp":"One PBIX, three environments, no code edits."},{"t":"Look up the last known exchange rate","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSales, ExchangeRates","guidance":"A","steps":["Rates only exist on Mondays. For each FactSales row you need the EUR rate from the most recent Monday on or before OrderDate.","Approach A (M): add WeekStart = Date.StartOfWeek([OrderDate], Day.Monday) to FactSales and merge on WeekStart = RateDate and Currency = \"EUR\".","Approach B (M, harder): buffer ExchangeRates with Table.Buffer, then per row List.Max of dates ≤ OrderDate. Compare refresh time.","Add Net Sales EUR = Net Sales × rate."],"exp":"99 of the 100 rows get a rate. The one order placed before the first Monday rate (5 Jan 2026) stays null until the business agrees on a fallback. Approach B is noticeably slower even at 100 rows; write down the two timings."},{"t":"Folding-safe incremental pattern","time":"20 min","ds":"FactSales via a SQL source if you have one, otherwise any date-filtered CSV","guidance":"A","steps":["Create RangeStart and RangeEnd Date/Time parameters.","Filter FactSales: OrderDate >= RangeStart and OrderDate < RangeEnd.","Check View Native Query at that step. If it folds, you are ready for incremental refresh; if not, move the filter earlier."],"exp":"You know which of your steps break folding (Table.AddColumn with a custom function usually does)."}],"int":[{"q":"What is the difference between Table.Buffer and List.Buffer and when do they help?","a":"Both load a table/list into memory once so repeated per-row lookups don't re-evaluate the source. They help in Table.AddColumn with lookups against a small table. They hurt when they stop folding on a large source."},{"q":"Explain \"each\" in M.","a":"each is syntactic sugar for a one-parameter function (_) => ..., and _ is the current row/item. each [Qty] * 2 equals (r) => r[Qty] * 2."},{"q":"How do you handle a merge where the key has different casing or trailing spaces?","a":"Normalise both sides before the merge (Text.Trim, Text.Lower) or use the comparer Comparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase as the key comparer argument of Table.NestedJoin. Never merge on raw text."},{"q":"When does a query stop folding? Give five common breakers.","a":"Custom functions per row, Table.Buffer, Text operations not supported by the source, adding an index column, changing type to a type the source doesn't map, merging with a non-foldable query, Table.Distinct on some sources, and anything after a step that already broke folding."},{"q":"Why does \"Enter Data\" not scale and what do you replace it with?","a":"It is a JSON blob embedded in the PBIX, cannot refresh, cannot be shared, has a size cap. Replace with a SharePoint list, a CSV in OneDrive, a Dataflow, or a proper database table."},{"q":"What is the difference between Table.SelectRows with a date filter and applying the filter on a parameter for incremental refresh?","a":"Functionally the same, but the Service rewrites RangeStart/RangeEnd per partition. If the filter uses any other expression, the partitions all load everything."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"After unpivoting SurveyWide correctly (Target excluded), row count is:","o":["12","36","48","24"],"a":1,"why":"12 stores × 3 month columns."},{"type":"mcq","q":"try Number.From(\"N/A\") otherwise null returns:","o":["0","an error","null","\"N/A\""],"a":2,"why":"try…otherwise catches the conversion error."},{"type":"task","q":"Write an M function that takes a table and a list of column names and returns the table with those columns trimmed, cleaned and capitalized. Apply it to RawOrdersExport.","hint":"Table.TransformColumns with List.Transform to build the transform list."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which step is most likely to stop query folding on SQL Server?","o":["Filter rows","Rename column","Add index column","Remove column"],"a":2,"why":"There is no deterministic SQL equivalent for a row index without an ORDER BY."}],"module":"intermediate"},{"id":"i-model","name":"Modeling: many-to-many, bridges and grain","ds":["FactSales","FactBudget","CustomerTargets","DimCustomer","DimEmployee"],"skills":["modeling"],"stage":"developer","refs":[{"title":"Many-to-many relationship guidance","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/guidance/relationships-many-to-many"},{"title":"Parent-child functions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/understanding-functions-for-parent-child-hierarchies-in-dax"}],"asg":[{"t":"Budget vs actual at different grains","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales, FactBudget","guidance":"A","steps":["FactBudget is at Month × Region × Category. FactSales is at Day × Product. They cannot join directly.","Create a DimCategory table = DISTINCT(DimProduct[Category]) and relate it to both DimProduct[Category] (1:*) and FactBudget[Category] (1:*).","Add YearMonth to your Dates table, and relate FactBudget[YearMonth] to a new DimMonth = DISTINCT(Dates[YearMonth]) which also filters Dates (1:*).","Relate DimRegion to FactBudget. Matrix: Category rows, YearMonth columns, Net Sales and Sum of BudgetAmount and Variance %."],"exp":"Every Category × Month cell shows both actual and budget. Product-level rows show budget blank (correct: budget is not defined at product grain)."},{"t":"Many-to-many with a bridge","time":"30 min","ds":"CustomerTargets, DimCustomer","guidance":"A","steps":["CustomerTargets keys on Segment + LoyaltyTier, which is not unique in either table.","Build a bridge: BridgeSegTier = SUMMARIZE(DimCustomer, DimCustomer[Segment], DimCustomer[LoyaltyTier]) plus a key column Segment & \"|\" & Tier.","Add the same key column to DimCustomer and CustomerTargets. Relate Bridge 1:* to both, with the Bridge → DimCustomer relationship set to bi-directional (only this one).","Table: Segment, LoyaltyTier, Net Sales, Sum of TargetRevenue.","Then do it again with a direct many-to-many relationship (cardinality *:*) and compare totals and behaviour."],"exp":"Both approaches give the same numbers per row; the *:* version shows a warning icon and behaves differently on the total row."},{"t":"Parent-child hierarchy","time":"30 min","ds":"DimEmployee, FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Add Path = PATH(DimEmployee[EmployeeKey], DimEmployee[ManagerKey]).","Add Level1 = LOOKUPVALUE(DimEmployee[EmployeeName], DimEmployee[EmployeeKey], PATHITEM([Path], 1, INTEGER)), and Level2, Level3, Level4.","Build a hierarchy Level1 → Level4 and a matrix of Net Sales by it.","Write Team Sales = CALCULATE([Net Sales], FILTER(ALL(DimEmployee), PATHCONTAINS(DimEmployee[Path], SELECTEDVALUE(DimEmployee[EmployeeKey])))) so a manager row includes their reports."],"exp":"Grace Hollis row = grand total. Dana Whitfield row = West total. Nina Kowalski (Finance) row has sales blank."},{"t":"Diagnose a bad grain","time":"15 min","ds":"FactInventory","guidance":"A","steps":["Load FactInventory and relate it to DimProduct and Dates.","Card: Sum of QuantityOnHand. Explain why the number is meaningless.","Do not fix it yet: that is the semi-additive assignment in Advanced DAX. Just write one sentence in a text box explaining the correct aggregation."],"exp":"The sentence contains the words \"last snapshot\" or \"last date\"."}],"int":[{"q":"How do you handle budget at month grain against sales at day grain?","a":"Create shared dimensions at the common grain (Category, Month, Region) that filter both facts. Never join facts to each other. Alternatively, allocate budget to days in Power Query if daily comparison is needed."},{"q":"Bridge table vs native many-to-many: which do you choose and why?","a":"Bridge with one bi-directional relationship is explicit, performs well, and totals behave predictably. Native *:* is quicker to build but totals ignore the relationship and it disables some features (e.g. no blank row, DAX like RELATED does not work)."},{"q":"What is a degenerate dimension?","a":"An attribute that lives on the fact because it has no other attributes, like OrderID. You slice by it directly from the fact rather than creating a one-column dimension."},{"q":"Explain the \"expanded table\" concept in DAX.","a":"Each table conceptually includes all columns of tables on the one side of its relationships. FactSales expanded includes DimProduct and DimCustomer columns; that is why RELATED works and why filters on a dimension filter the fact."},{"q":"When is a snapshot fact table the right design?","a":"When the business asks \"what was the balance/level at a point in time\" (inventory, account balances, headcount). Sum across time is meaningless; use semi-additive measures."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"FactBudget and FactSales both have RegionKey. Correct model:","o":["Join FactSales to FactBudget on RegionKey","DimRegion filters both facts","Merge them in Power Query","Use a *:* between them"],"a":1,"why":"Conformed dimensions filter multiple facts; facts never join to facts."},{"type":"mcq","q":"PATH(EmployeeKey, ManagerKey) for Lily Chang (8) returns:","o":["\"8\"","\"1|2|6|8\"","\"8|6|2|1\"","\"2|6|8\""],"a":1,"why":"PATH lists ancestors from the root to the item."},{"type":"task","q":"Build the bridge for CustomerTargets and report the Q1 target versus Net Sales for Consumer × Gold.","hint":"If Net Sales is blank, the bridge → DimCustomer relationship is not bi-directional."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which relationship direction is required for the bridge pattern to work?","o":["Bridge ← Fact","Bridge ↔ Dimension (both)","Fact ↔ Bridge","No relationships, use TREATAS"],"a":1,"why":"The dimension must be filtered through the bridge so the fact receives the filter."}],"module":"intermediate"},{"id":"i-dax","name":"DAX: filter context, time intelligence and iterators","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct","DimCustomer","FactBudget"],"skills":["dax"],"stage":"developer","refs":[{"title":"CALCULATE","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/calculate-function-dax"},{"title":"Time intelligence functions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/time-intelligence-functions-dax"},{"title":"Use variables to improve your DAX formulas","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/best-practices/dax-variables"}],"asg":[{"t":"CALCULATE modifiers, all of them","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales, DimProduct","guidance":"A","steps":["Write and put side by side in a table by Category with a Region slicer set to West: [Net Sales], CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALL(DimProduct)), CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALLSELECTED(DimProduct)), CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALLEXCEPT(DimProduct, DimProduct[Category])), CALCULATE([Net Sales], REMOVEFILTERS()), CALCULATE([Net Sales], KEEPFILTERS(DimProduct[Category] = \"Water\")).","Now add a visual-level filter Category ≠ Apparel and watch which columns change.","Write a one-line comment above each measure describing which filters it keeps."],"exp":"ALL ignores the visual filter; ALLSELECTED respects it. KEEPFILTERS gives blank on non-Water rows instead of the Water number."},{"t":"Time intelligence set","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales, Dates","guidance":"A","steps":["Extend FactSales mentally: it only spans Jan–Mar 2026, so YoY will be blank. That is fine; you are testing the pattern, not the data.","Write: Sales MTD = TOTALMTD([Net Sales], Dates[Date]), Sales QTD, Sales PM = CALCULATE([Net Sales], DATEADD(Dates[Date], -1, MONTH)), MoM % = DIVIDE([Net Sales] - [Sales PM], [Sales PM]), Sales Rolling 30 = CALCULATE([Net Sales], DATESINPERIOD(Dates[Date], MAX(Dates[Date]), -30, DAY)).","Line chart by Date with Net Sales and Sales Rolling 30.","Break it: remove the \"mark as date table\" flag and observe what happens to Sales PM. Restore it."],"exp":"Feb MoM % is computed. Sales PM for January is blank. Rolling 30 is smooth. Unmarking the date table does not break these measures because you referenced Dates[Date] directly; then delete the relationship and watch them break."},{"t":"Iterators and row context","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSales, DimCustomer","guidance":"A","steps":["Write Avg Sales per Customer = AVERAGEX(VALUES(DimCustomer[CustomerKey]), [Net Sales]) and compare to DIVIDE([Net Sales], [Customers Buying]).","Write Best Product Sales = MAXX(VALUES(DimProduct[ProductName]), [Net Sales]) and Best Product = the name, using TOPN(1, VALUES(DimProduct[ProductName]), [Net Sales]) wrapped in MAXX to return a text.","Write Customer Rank = RANKX(ALL(DimCustomer[CustomerName]), [Net Sales], , DESC, DENSE). Put it in a table by CustomerName. Then make it respect the slicer by swapping ALL for ALLSELECTED.","Write Customers Over 500 = COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES(DimCustomer[CustomerKey]), [Net Sales] > 500))."],"exp":"Rank 1 customer is unique. Customers Over 500 total is not the sum across regions (a customer can appear in two regions if reps cross regions)."},{"t":"Variables and debugging","time":"20 min","ds":"FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Rewrite MoM % with VAR cur, VAR prev, VAR delta and RETURN. Add a temporary RETURN prev to inspect the intermediate value, then restore.","Write a measure that returns a text: \"Net \" & FORMAT([Net Sales], \"$#,##0\") & \" across \" & [Orders] & \" orders\". Put it in a card.","Install DAX Studio, connect to your open PBIX, and run: EVALUATE SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(DimProduct[Category], \"Sales\", [Net Sales]). Then turn on Server Timings and note the SE vs FE split."],"exp":"You can state the FE and SE milliseconds for one query."},{"t":"Budget variance the right way","time":"20 min","ds":"FactBudget, FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Budget = SUM(FactBudget[BudgetAmount]). Variance = [Net Sales] - [Budget]. Variance % = DIVIDE([Variance], [Budget]).","Attainment Status = SWITCH(TRUE(), ISBLANK([Budget]), \"No budget\", [Variance %] >= 0, \"On target\", [Variance %] >= -0.1, \"Watch\", \"Behind\").","Use Attainment Status for conditional formatting (field value) on a matrix."],"exp":"Product-level rows show \"No budget\" because budget is only at category grain."}],"int":[{"q":"ALL vs ALLSELECTED vs REMOVEFILTERS: one sentence each.","a":"ALL removes filters from the given table/columns. REMOVEFILTERS is ALL restricted to being a CALCULATE modifier (clearer intent, cannot be used as a table). ALLSELECTED restores the filters from outside the visual (slicers) while removing the visual's own row/column filters."},{"q":"Why does a measure inside SUMX need CALCULATE, and why don't you write it?","a":"Row context does not filter. A measure reference is implicitly wrapped in CALCULATE (context transition), which turns the current row into a filter. That is why AVERAGEX(VALUES(Customer), [Net Sales]) works; writing SUM(FactSales[...]) inside would ignore the row."},{"q":"What does DATEADD do when the previous period has no data, and how does that differ from SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR?","a":"DATEADD returns the set of shifted dates that exist in the date table; if the fact has no rows the measure is blank. SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR is DATEADD(-1, YEAR). Both require a proper date table. PARALLELPERIOD returns whole periods instead of the same dates."},{"q":"RANKX gives all 1s. Why?","a":"The second argument is evaluated in the current filter context, so every row ranks against itself. Use ALL/ALLSELECTED on the column being ranked, and make sure the expression is a measure (context transition) not a raw column."},{"q":"What is the difference between VALUES and DISTINCT?","a":"VALUES includes the blank row created by referential-integrity violations; DISTINCT does not. In iterators over dimension keys the difference can move a total."},{"q":"Explain context transition and one case where it hurts performance.","a":"When a measure (or CALCULATE) is evaluated in row context, the row values become filters. Inside SUMX over a 10-million-row fact, calling a measure per row causes 10 million context transitions and a huge formula-engine cost; rewrite with column arithmetic or pre-aggregated tables."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALLSELECTED(DimProduct)) in a table by Category with a visual filter Category ≠ Apparel and slicer Region = West shows:","o":["All-region, all-category total","West total excluding Apparel, on every row","West total including Apparel","The row's own value"],"a":1,"why":"ALLSELECTED keeps slicer and visual filters but removes the row's category."},{"type":"mcq","q":"TOTALMTD([Net Sales], Dates[Date]) is equivalent to:","o":["CALCULATE([Net Sales], DATESMTD(Dates[Date]))","CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALL(Dates))","SUMX(Dates, [Net Sales])","CALCULATE([Net Sales], DATEADD(Dates[Date],-1,MONTH))"],"a":0,"why":"TOTALMTD is shorthand for CALCULATE with DATESMTD."},{"type":"task","q":"Write a measure \"Top 3 Products Sales\" that returns Net Sales for the top 3 products by Net Sales within the current filter context, and a second measure \"Top 3 Share\" = its share of total. Verify Top 3 Share for Camping.","hint":"CALCULATE([Net Sales], TOPN(3, VALUES(DimProduct[ProductName]), [Net Sales]))."},{"type":"mcq","q":"A FILTER over FactSales (100 rows) calling [Net Sales] per row performs:","o":["100 storage-engine scans, very fast","100 context transitions, slow at scale","One scan","It errors"],"a":1,"why":"Each measure call in row context triggers context transition; fine at 100 rows, fatal at 10 million."}],"module":"intermediate"},{"id":"i-viz","name":"Interactive reports: bookmarks, drillthrough, tooltips, field parameters","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct","DimCustomer"],"skills":["visuals","communication"],"stage":"developer","refs":[{"title":"Drillthrough","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-drillthrough"},{"title":"Field parameters","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/power-bi-field-parameters"}],"asg":[{"t":"Drillthrough with a back button","time":"25 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Create page \"Customer Detail\" with a drillthrough field CustomerName. Add a table of their orders, a card for their Net Sales, and a line chart by date.","Turn on \"Keep all filters\". Add a back button (auto-created) and style it.","From the summary page, right-click a customer bar → Drillthrough. Verify the Region slicer selection is carried over.","Add a second drillthrough field ProductName to the same page and observe it now requires either."],"exp":"Right-click menu shows \"Customer Detail\". Back button returns to the source page."},{"t":"Report page tooltip","time":"20 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["New page, Page information → Allow use as tooltip, size Tooltip.","Add a card Net Sales, a small bar chart of SubCategory, and a text measure \"X orders, Y customers\".","On the summary page, set the Category bar chart Tooltip → Report page → your page."],"exp":"Hovering over \"Water\" shows Water-only numbers inside the tooltip."},{"t":"Field parameters for a self-service chart","time":"20 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Modeling → New parameter → Fields. Add Net Sales, Orders, Margin %, Total Qty as one parameter \"Measure Picker\".","Create a second field parameter \"Axis Picker\" with Category, RegionName, Segment, MonthName.","One clustered bar chart driven by both parameters, two slicers to switch them."],"exp":"Sixteen chart combinations from one visual. Look at the generated DAX for the parameter table and explain the third column."},{"t":"Bookmark toggle done right","time":"25 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Two visuals stacked exactly on top of each other: a column chart and a table of the same data.","Two bookmarks \"Show chart\" / \"Show table\" that only change Display (Data and Current page unchecked), created with the Selection pane.","Two buttons whose visible state is swapped by the same bookmarks so the active one looks pressed.","Group the four objects and name the group; ungroup and note what happens to the bookmarks."],"exp":"Clicking either button never resets slicers. Bookmarks have Data unchecked."},{"t":"Dynamic titles and formatting measures","time":"15 min","ds":"Full star","guidance":"A","steps":["Title measure = \"Net sales for \" & IF(ISFILTERED(DimRegion[RegionName]), SELECTEDVALUE(DimRegion[RegionName], \"multiple regions\"), \"all regions\") & \" – \" & FORMAT(MAX(Dates[Date]), \"MMM yyyy\").","Use it as the fx title on a chart.","Colour measure = IF([Margin %] < 0.4, \"#B23A2E\", \"#1F7A4D\") used as fx on a bar colour."],"exp":"Title changes with the slicer. Bars change colour without conditional formatting rules."}],"int":[{"q":"Bookmark \"Data\" checkbox: when do you leave it on, when off?","a":"On when the bookmark is meant to restore a filter state (a saved view). Off when it only toggles visibility or a visual swap; otherwise the user's slicer selections reset every time they click the button."},{"q":"Drillthrough vs tooltip vs drill down: when each?","a":"Drill down: same visual, hierarchy levels. Drillthrough: navigate to a detail page for one item. Tooltip page: peek at detail without leaving. Choose the least disruptive one that answers the question."},{"q":"What is the hidden third column in a field parameter table used for?","a":"It is the sort/order column (and there is also the field reference stored via NAMEOF). You can add more columns, e.g. a group column, to build grouped slicers."},{"q":"How do you conditionally show a visual based on a slicer selection?","a":"Field parameters or a measure-driven visual filter (e.g. a measure returning 1 or 0 as a visual-level filter) or bookmarks. Visuals cannot be hidden by a measure directly; use a transparent overlay shape whose fill is a colour measure with 0% alpha, or the page-navigation trick."},{"q":"Why is a 30-visual page slow even though the model is small?","a":"Each visual issues at least one query and they compete for the formula engine; slicers with cross-filtering issue queries per interaction. Reduce visuals, combine cards into one multi-row card or matrix, disable unnecessary interactions."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"\"Keep all filters\" on drillthrough means:","o":["Slicers on the target page are locked","Filters from the source page context are carried over","The target page ignores filters","Filters are saved to a bookmark"],"a":1,"why":"It passes the full filter context of the clicked data point, not only the drillthrough field."},{"type":"mcq","q":"A field parameter is:","o":["A Power Query parameter","A calculated table with NAMEOF references usable in visuals","A what-if slider","A bookmark group"],"a":1,"why":"Field parameters are calculated tables with special metadata."},{"type":"task","q":"Build a page where one button toggles between \"Actual\" and \"Budget\" in a single matrix without resetting any slicer. Prove it by selecting Region = East, toggling twice, and confirming East stays selected.","hint":"Two bookmarks with Data unchecked, or one field parameter slicer styled as buttons."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which formatting property can be driven by a measure returning a hex colour?","o":["Only background of cells","Most colour properties with an fx button, including bar colours and titles","None","Only conditional formatting rules"],"a":1,"why":"Any property with fx accepts a field value."}],"module":"intermediate"},{"id":"i-rls","name":"Row-level security","ds":["UserRegionMapping","DimRegion","FactSales","DimEmployee"],"skills":["security"],"stage":"developer","why":{"matters":"Security is the one defect a company cannot fix with an apology: a manager seeing another region's payroll is a reportable incident.","failure":"A page filter or a hidden visual is used as \"security\"; anyone with Build permission or Analyze in Excel sees everything.","use":"Whenever different people may see different rows of the same model.","avoid":"When groups need entirely different models anyway, or when security must hold for direct SQL access too (secure the source as well)."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Row-level security docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Row-level security with Power BI","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/security/service-admin-row-level-security"},{"title":"RLS guidance","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/guidance/rls-guidance"}],"asg":[{"t":"Static roles","time":"20 min","ds":"DimRegion","guidance":"A","steps":["Manage roles → new role \"West\" with DAX filter on DimRegion: [RegionName] = \"West\". Create South, East, Central the same way.","View as → West. Note that the Region slicer now shows only West.","Publish, add a test user to the West role in the Service, open the report as them."],"exp":"Cards show West totals only. The user cannot see other regions even by editing the report."},{"t":"Dynamic RLS with a mapping table","time":"40 min","ds":"UserRegionMapping, DimRegion","guidance":"A","steps":["Load UserRegionMapping. Relate UserRegionMapping[RegionKey] → DimRegion[RegionKey]? No: the mapping is many rows per user, so relate DimRegion (1) → UserRegionMapping (*) and set the relationship to bi-directional with \"Apply security filter in both directions\" on.","Role \"Dynamic\": filter on UserRegionMapping: [UserEmail] = USERPRINCIPALNAME().","Handle the \"All\" row: change the DimRegion filter instead: VAR u = USERPRINCIPALNAME() RETURN CONTAINS(UserRegionMapping, UserRegionMapping[UserEmail], u, UserRegionMapping[RegionKey], DimRegion[RegionKey]) || CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserRegionMapping, [UserEmail] = u && [AccessLevel] = \"All\"))) > 0","View as → Other user → nina.kowalski@northwind.example. Then grace.hollis@."],"exp":"Nina sees West and East only. Grace sees all four. Dana sees West."},{"t":"RLS by org hierarchy","time":"30 min","ds":"DimEmployee, FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Role \"MyTeam\": filter DimEmployee with PATHCONTAINS(DimEmployee[Path], LOOKUPVALUE(DimEmployee[EmployeeKey], DimEmployee[Email], USERPRINCIPALNAME())).","View as dana.whitfield@: she should see herself and everyone under her.","View as lily.chang@: she sees only herself."],"exp":"Dana: 5 employees' sales. Lily: 1."},{"t":"Test that RLS cannot be bypassed","time":"15 min","ds":"Full model","guidance":"A","steps":["As the restricted user, try Analyze in Excel and try building a new report on the model (needs Build). Confirm RLS still applies.","Add a measure CALCULATE([Net Sales], ALL(DimRegion)) and confirm it still returns only the allowed regions.","Publish to a second workspace and note that role membership does not travel with it."],"exp":"ALL does not remove RLS filters; role membership must be reassigned in each workspace."}],"int":[{"q":"Why can ALL() not bypass RLS?","a":"RLS filters are applied at the storage layer before any DAX runs; they are not part of the filter context DAX manipulates."},{"q":"Static vs dynamic RLS: trade-offs.","a":"Static: simple, one role per group, membership managed in the Service, breaks when groups change. Dynamic: one role, mapping table maintained by the business, needs USERPRINCIPALNAME and a bi-directional security filter, and the mapping must be refreshed."},{"q":"What happens if a user is in two roles?","a":"Filters are combined with OR: they see the union. Roles never intersect."},{"q":"Does RLS apply to workspace Admins, Members and Contributors?","a":"No. It applies only to users with Viewer role or with read permission via app/share. Anyone who can edit the model is exempt."},{"q":"How does RLS interact with a bi-directional relationship?","a":"Security filters only flow through a bi-directional relationship if \"Apply security filter in both directions\" is checked; otherwise the mapping-table role filters nothing on the fact side."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"A user is in roles West and East. They see:","o":["Nothing","West only","West and East","Everything"],"a":2,"why":"Multiple roles combine with OR."},{"type":"mcq","q":"USERPRINCIPALNAME() in Desktop returns:","o":["Blank","Your signed-in Desktop account email","The workspace owner","\"admin\""],"a":1,"why":"It returns the current user; View as → Other user lets you impersonate."},{"type":"task","q":"Implement dynamic RLS for UserRegionMapping including the \"All\" row. Prove Nina sees exactly two regions with a screenshot of View as.","hint":"If Nina sees all regions, the \"All\" check is missing a filter on AccessLevel; if she sees none, the relationship isn't bi-directional for security."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Workspace Member opens an RLS-secured report. They see:","o":["Their role's rows","Everything","Nothing","An error"],"a":1,"why":"Edit-capable roles bypass RLS."}],"module":"intermediate"},{"id":"i-service","name":"Service: gateways, refresh, workspaces and apps","ds":["FactSales"],"skills":["service","governance"],"stage":"developer","verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Gateway, workspace and refresh docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"What is an on-premises data gateway?","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/service-gateway-onprem"},{"title":"Workspaces in Power BI","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/collaborate-share/service-new-workspaces"},{"title":"Troubleshoot refresh scenarios","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/refresh-troubleshooting-refresh-scenarios"}],"asg":[{"t":"Install and use a gateway","time":"40 min","ds":"A local CSV or SQL Express","guidance":"A","steps":["Install the on-premises data gateway (standard mode) on your machine. Register it.","Add a data source (File or SQL). Map the report's data source to it in the semantic model settings.","Schedule refresh. Then stop the gateway service and trigger refresh: read the exact error.","Add a second admin to the gateway."],"exp":"Refresh succeeds with gateway online and fails with a gateway-offline message when it is not."},{"t":"Workspace strategy","time":"20 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Create workspaces Northwind-Dev, Northwind-Test, Northwind-Prod. Publish to Dev.","Move the semantic model to a separate workspace \"Northwind-Models\" and make the report connect live to it (Desktop → Get Data → Power BI semantic models). Republish.","Grant Build on the model to a colleague and have them create a report in their own workspace."],"exp":"One model, two reports in different workspaces. Deleting the report does not delete the model."},{"t":"Refresh diagnostics","time":"20 min","ds":"Any","guidance":"A","steps":["Open refresh history and download the refresh log.","Set failure notifications to a colleague.","Configure refresh 8 times a day and note the Pro limit; then read the capacity limit in the settings tooltip."],"exp":"You can name the daily refresh limit for Pro and for capacity."},{"t":"App with audiences","time":"20 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Create an App with two audiences: Managers (all pages) and Reps (one page only).","Add a navigation section and a link to an external page.","Publish, then update one visual, republish the report, update the App. Observe the difference."],"exp":"Rep audience cannot see the manager page even by URL."}],"int":[{"q":"Personal mode vs standard mode gateway.","a":"Personal: one user, no sharing, no DirectQuery, no dataflows. Standard: shared, clustered, supports DirectQuery/live and dataflows, needs a service account and admins."},{"q":"How do you avoid 50 reports each with their own copy of the model?","a":"Publish one certified semantic model in a models workspace, give Build to authors, and have every report live-connect to it. Use endorsement (Promoted/Certified) so authors find it."},{"q":"Scheduled refresh keeps failing at 6:00 but works manually. Where do you look?","a":"Gateway online status at that hour, source maintenance windows, credential expiry, the log around that time, timezone of the schedule, and whether the manual refresh used a different (cached) credential."},{"q":"What is the difference between \"Update app\" and \"Republish\"?","a":"Republish from Desktop updates the workspace content; Update app pushes workspace content to app consumers. Both are needed for consumers to see a change."},{"q":"Where do you put a shared date table and shared measures so every team reuses them?","a":"In the shared semantic model. Reports live-connected to it can add report-level measures but not tables, which forces consistency."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"A DirectQuery report to on-prem SQL requires:","o":["Personal gateway","Standard gateway","No gateway","A dataflow"],"a":1,"why":"DirectQuery is not supported by personal mode."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Live connection to a shared model lets you:","o":["Add tables","Add report-level measures","Edit Power Query","Change relationships"],"a":1,"why":"Live connections are read-only on the model except report measures."},{"type":"task","q":"Set up gateway refresh for a local CSV, break it, fix it, and document the three settings you had to touch in the Service.","hint":"Gateway mapping, data source credentials, schedule."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Which workspace role is the minimum to publish an App?","o":["Viewer","Contributor","Member","Admin"],"a":2,"why":"Contributors can publish reports but not apps by default."}],"module":"intermediate"}]},
{"id":"advanced","kind":"level","order":3,"cls":"adv","name":"Advanced","years":"Year 3 – 5","tagline":"Performance tuning, calculation groups, composite models, deployment, Fabric and governance.","seo":"Advanced Power BI practice: DAX Studio and VertiPaq tuning, calculation groups, composite models, PBIP and Git, Fabric Direct Lake and governance.","intro":"At this level the questions are \"why is it slow\", \"how do 40 reports share one model without breaking\", and \"how do we ship changes safely\". Tools: DAX Studio, Tabular Editor 2 or 3, VertiPaq Analyzer, a Fabric trial, Git.","topics":[{"id":"a-perf","name":"Performance: VertiPaq, query plans, aggregations, incremental refresh","ds":["FactSales","WebEvents"],"skills":["performance"],"stage":"senior","why":{"matters":"Slow reports stop being used, and a model that is too big costs real capacity money every hour.","failure":"An executive page takes 18 seconds every Monday because one measure iterates the whole fact table per cell.","use":"Measure first: Performance Analyzer, DAX query view and Server Timings tell you whether the time is in visuals, the formula engine or the storage engine.","avoid":"Optimising without a baseline. Every change needs a before and after number."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Performance Analyzer, DAX query view, incremental refresh docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20); DP-600 (2026-10-19)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Optimization guide for Power BI","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/guidance/power-bi-optimization"},{"title":"Performance Analyzer","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-performance-analyzer"},{"title":"Incremental refresh overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/incremental-refresh-overview"}],"asg":[{"t":"Make a big fact and measure it","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["In Power Query, reference FactSales and cross-join it with a 1,000-row list (List.Numbers) to get 100,000 rows; add a random offset to dates. Name it FactSalesBig.","Open DAX Studio → Advanced → View Metrics (VertiPaq Analyzer). Record total model size and the top 3 columns by size.","Change SalesKey to not loaded (remove it), and change UnitPrice from Decimal to Fixed Decimal. Re-run metrics. Record the size difference.","Split OrderDate/ShipDate into Date only (remove time). Record again."],"exp":"A table with before/after sizes. The high-cardinality key column dominates size; removing it saves the most."},{"t":"Read a query plan","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSalesBig","guidance":"A","steps":["Write the slow version: Customers Over 500 Slow = COUNTROWS(FILTER(FactSalesBig, [Net Sales] > 500)).","In DAX Studio, Server Timings on, run a matrix query using it. Record FE ms, SE ms, number of SE queries, and whether CallbackDataID appears.","Rewrite: COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES(DimCustomer[CustomerKey]), [Net Sales] > 500)). Re-run and compare.","Rewrite once more with SUMMARIZE + a filter on a pre-computed column; compare."],"exp":"Version 1 shows one SE query per row or a CallbackDataID; version 2 is 10× fewer SE queries."},{"t":"Aggregation table","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSalesBig","guidance":"A","steps":["Create AggSalesMonthCat in Power Query: group FactSalesBig by YearMonth, Category, RegionKey with Sum Quantity, Sum Amount, Count rows.","Set FactSalesBig to DirectQuery (or keep Import and just practise the mapping), AggSalesMonthCat to Import. Manage aggregations: map each column.","In DAX Studio, run a query by Category and check the \"Aggregation hit\" in the query plan event; then run by ProductName and confirm it misses."],"exp":"One query hits the agg (Category grain), one misses (Product grain)."},{"t":"Incremental refresh end to end","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSalesBig via SQL or a partitioned CSV folder","guidance":"A","steps":["RangeStart/RangeEnd parameters; filter step that folds.","Incremental refresh policy: archive 2 years, refresh 3 days, detect data changes on a ModifiedDate column if you have one.","Publish, refresh, then in SSMS or Tabular Editor via XMLA endpoint (needs capacity/PPU) look at the partitions created.","Simulate a late-arriving fact and confirm it is not picked up outside the refresh window. Then fix with a longer window."],"exp":"Partition list shows year, quarter, month and day partitions."},{"t":"Storage engine friendly DAX","time":"30 min","ds":"WebEvents","guidance":"A","steps":["Write Sessions With Purchase = CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(WebEvents[SessionID]), WebEvents[EventType] = \"Purchase\").","Write Conversion Rate = DIVIDE([Sessions With Purchase], DISTINCTCOUNT(WebEvents[SessionID])).","Write Avg Session Minutes two ways: (a) AVERAGEX(VALUES(SessionID), DATEDIFF(CALCULATE(MIN(EventTime)), CALCULATE(MAX(EventTime)), MINUTE)) and (b) with a calculated column SessionStart via EARLIER, then a measure. Compare the query plan cost and model size."],"exp":"You can articulate when to pay the cost at refresh (column) versus at query (measure)."}],"int":[{"q":"How does VertiPaq compress data, and what is the single biggest lever?","a":"Dictionary encoding per column plus run-length encoding on the sorted values. Cardinality is the lever: fewer distinct values → smaller dictionary and longer runs. So remove high-cardinality columns, round decimals, split datetime into date and time."},{"q":"Formula engine vs storage engine: what runs where?","a":"SE (VertiPaq) executes simple scans, filters and aggregations in parallel and is fast. FE is single-threaded and handles everything the SE cannot: iterators calling measures, complex conditions, TOPN over measures. Optimising = pushing work from FE to SE."},{"q":"What is a CallbackDataID and why is it bad?","a":"The SE calling back into the FE per row because an expression inside an iterator cannot be executed by SE (e.g. IF, DIVIDE with a measure). It serialises the scan and defeats the SE cache."},{"q":"Aggregations: when do they not help?","a":"When the query grain is finer than the agg table, when a measure uses DISTINCTCOUNT (needs the detail unless you build a count-distinct agg with GroupBy), or when RLS filters columns not in the agg table."},{"q":"Incremental refresh: what happens on the first refresh after publishing, and how do you avoid a timeout?","a":"The first refresh loads all historical partitions and can time out. Publish the model with no partitions loaded, then refresh partitions in batches via XMLA (Tabular Editor / SSMS), or use bootstrap \"Apply refresh policy\" without data first."},{"q":"Give three model-level performance rules you enforce in code review.","a":"No calculated columns on facts unless justified, no bi-directional relationships without a written reason, integer keys not text, dates without time, measures over iterators over facts, hide and remove unused columns, Fixed Decimal for currency."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"Which change reduces model size most?","o":["Rename columns","Remove a unique integer key column from a 100k-row fact","Change text to uppercase","Add a hierarchy"],"a":1,"why":"Unique keys have a dictionary as large as the table."},{"type":"mcq","q":"FILTER(FactSales, [Net Sales] > 500) versus FILTER(VALUES(DimCustomer[CustomerKey]), [Net Sales] > 500):","o":["Same cost","First is far more expensive due to per-row context transition","Second is more expensive","Both are storage-engine only"],"a":1,"why":"Iterating 100k fact rows with a measure creates 100k context transitions."},{"type":"task","q":"Produce a VertiPaq Analyzer before/after table for FactSalesBig with at least three optimisations and the % reduction of each.","hint":"Key removal, Fixed Decimal, date/time split, removing unused columns."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Detect data changes in incremental refresh requires:","o":["A date column","A datetime column such as LastModified that folds","Nothing","A primary key"],"a":1,"why":"The policy compares MAX(LastModified) per partition."}],"module":"advanced"},{"id":"a-dax","name":"Advanced DAX: calculation groups, TREATAS, semi-additive, virtual tables","ds":["FactSales","FactInventory","FactBudget","ExchangeRates"],"skills":["dax","modeling"],"stage":"senior","why":{"matters":"Advanced DAX patterns are how one certified model answers hundreds of questions without hundreds of near-duplicate measures.","failure":"A semi-additive stock measure sums weekly snapshots and inventory looks ten times larger than it is.","use":"Calculation groups for repeated transformations (time intelligence, currency); window functions for running totals and comparisons.","avoid":"Clever DAX that nobody else on the team can maintain. Prefer visual calculations for one-off visual math."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Calculation groups, window functions, visual calculations docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Calculation groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/calculation-groups"},{"title":"WINDOW function","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/window-function-dax"},{"title":"Visual calculations overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/desktop-visual-calculations-overview"}],"asg":[{"t":"Semi-additive inventory","time":"30 min","ds":"FactInventory, Dates","guidance":"A","steps":["Stock On Hand = CALCULATE(SUM(FactInventory[QuantityOnHand]), LASTDATE(FactInventory[SnapshotDate])) — put it in a matrix by MonthName. Notice it uses the last snapshot date within each month.","Now the problem: LASTDATE over Dates gives blank for days with no snapshot. Rewrite with LASTNONBLANK: CALCULATE(SUM(QuantityOnHand), LASTNONBLANK(Dates[Date], CALCULATE(SUM(FactInventory[QuantityOnHand])))).","Add Below Reorder = COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES(DimProduct[ProductKey]), [Stock On Hand] < CALCULATE(MAX(FactInventory[ReorderPoint]))))."],"exp":"Matrix by month shows the last week's level, not a sum. Below Reorder flags Hydro Filter Bottle at the end of January and Ridge Runner Boots at the end of February (both under their reorder point of 30); nothing is below reorder at the end of March."},{"t":"Calculation group for time intelligence","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales, Dates","guidance":"A","steps":["Tabular Editor 2 → New Calculation Group \"Time Calc\" with items: Current = SELECTEDMEASURE(), PM = CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE(), DATEADD(Dates[Date], -1, MONTH)), MoM % = DIVIDE(SELECTEDMEASURE() - CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE(), DATEADD(Dates[Date], -1, MONTH)), CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE(), DATEADD(Dates[Date], -1, MONTH))), MTD = CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE(), DATESMTD(Dates[Date])).","Set a format string expression on MoM % to \"0.0%\" and on the others to SELECTEDMEASUREFORMATSTRING().","Save to the model. Matrix: rows Category, columns Time Calc, values Net Sales, then switch value to Orders. Both get all four variants without new measures.","Set precedence and observe what happens when you add a second calculation group \"Currency\" (below)."],"exp":"Format strings switch correctly per column. Implicit measures stop working (turn on Discourage implicit measures)."},{"t":"Currency conversion calculation group","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSales, ExchangeRates","guidance":"A","steps":["Relate ExchangeRates to Dates on RateDate (inactive is fine). Build a rate lookup measure: Rate = VAR c = SELECTEDVALUE(Currency[Code]) VAR dte = MAX(Dates[Date]) RETURN CALCULATE(MAX(ExchangeRates[RateToUSD]), ExchangeRates[Currency] = c, ExchangeRates[RateDate] <= dte, LASTDATE(...)) — or a simpler LASTNONBLANK pattern.","Calculation group \"Currency\": USD = SELECTEDMEASURE(), Selected = SUMX(VALUES(Dates[Date]), CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE()) / [Rate]) where Rate is the last known rate for that date.","Currency slicer from a disconnected table. Check Net Sales in EUR for January."],"exp":"Converting per day then summing gives a different number than converting the monthly total by one rate; you can explain which is correct."},{"t":"TREATAS and virtual relationships","time":"30 min","ds":"FactBudget, FactSales","guidance":"A","steps":["Delete the DimCategory relationship to FactBudget from the Intermediate model.","Budget via TREATAS = CALCULATE(SUM(FactBudget[BudgetAmount]), TREATAS(VALUES(DimProduct[Category]), FactBudget[Category]), TREATAS(VALUES(Dates[YearMonth]), FactBudget[YearMonth])).","Compare against the physical relationship version in DAX Studio timings.","Do the same with CROSSFILTER to temporarily change a relationship direction inside a measure."],"exp":"Same numbers; TREATAS is slower on large budgets but has no model impact."},{"t":"Virtual tables and window functions","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSales, DimCustomer","guidance":"A","steps":["Customer ABC Class = VAR t = ADDCOLUMNS(ALLSELECTED(DimCustomer[CustomerKey]), \"@s\", [Net Sales]) VAR total = SUMX(t, [@s]) VAR cur = [Net Sales] VAR cum = SUMX(FILTER(t, [@s] >= cur), [@s]) RETURN SWITCH(TRUE(), DIVIDE(cum,total) <= 0.7, \"A\", DIVIDE(cum,total) <= 0.9, \"B\", \"C\").","Rewrite the running total with WINDOW: Running Sales = CALCULATE([Net Sales], WINDOW(1, ABS, 0, REL, ALLSELECTED(DimCustomer[CustomerName]), ORDERBY([Net Sales], DESC))).","Use OFFSET to get the previous customer's sales in a sorted table, and RANK for the position.","Explain in a comment why WINDOW cannot be wrapped in a non-trivial FILTER."],"exp":"A/B/C classification sums to 100% of customers; Running Sales in the last row equals the total."}],"int":[{"q":"Calculation group precedence: what does it decide?","a":"When two groups apply to the same cell, the higher-precedence group's expression is applied last (outermost). Time intelligence normally wraps currency conversion, so Time Calc gets higher precedence."},{"q":"LASTDATE vs LASTNONBLANK vs MAX for semi-additive measures.","a":"LASTDATE returns the last date in the current date filter even if there is no data. LASTNONBLANK scans for the last date where the expression is non-blank. MAX(date) is faster than LASTDATE but returns a scalar, so wrap it in a filter. Prefer LASTNONBLANKVALUE for a single column."},{"q":"TREATAS vs relationship: three differences.","a":"TREATAS is per-measure and has no model change; relationships are global and faster. TREATAS handles multi-column mappings with no key. Relationships propagate RLS; TREATAS does not filter other measures automatically."},{"q":"What does SELECTEDMEASUREFORMATSTRING() solve?","a":"Calculation items that return the base measure should keep its format; without it every item defaults to the group's format string and Net Sales loses its $."},{"q":"When do window functions (WINDOW, OFFSET, INDEX, RANK) beat the classic EARLIER / FILTER patterns?","a":"Whenever you need ordered access (previous row, running total, top-N within group). They are optimised for it and readable; the classic patterns are O(n²) iterators."},{"q":"How do you handle a currency conversion where the rate is missing for a date?","a":"Use the last known rate before that date (LASTNONBLANK pattern or a forward-fill in Power Query). Surface missing rates as a data-quality measure rather than silently returning blank."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"Summing FactInventory[QuantityOnHand] over 10 weeks for one product gives:","o":["The current stock","10× the average stock, meaningless","Zero","An error"],"a":1,"why":"Snapshot facts are non-additive across time."},{"type":"mcq","q":"With calculation groups present, implicit measures (dragging a column):","o":["Work normally","Are ignored by calculation items and should be disabled","Become measures","Error"],"a":1,"why":"Calculation items only apply to explicit measures; discourage implicit measures in the model."},{"type":"task","q":"Build the Time Calc group and prove MTD works for Net Sales and for Orders without writing extra measures. Show the matrix with 8 columns.","hint":"If Orders MTD shows a $ sign, the format string expression is wrong."},{"type":"mcq","q":"TREATAS(VALUES(DimProduct[Category]), FactBudget[Category]) fails silently if:","o":["Category has more than 4 values","The text values differ in case or spacing","FactBudget has more rows","Dates is not marked"],"a":1,"why":"TREATAS matches values exactly; \"camping\" ≠ \"Camping\"."}],"module":"advanced"},{"id":"a-composite","name":"Composite models, DirectQuery and hybrid tables","ds":["FactSales","DimProduct"],"skills":["modeling","performance","architecture"],"stage":"senior","why":{"matters":"Storage mode is an architecture decision: it fixes latency, cost and which DAX features you can use.","failure":"A DirectQuery model \"for real-time\" hammers the ERP database at 9am and the operations team blocks the service account.","use":"Import by default; DirectQuery or hybrid tables when latency truly matters; Dual for shared dimensions; Direct Lake when data already lives in OneLake.","avoid":"Choosing DirectQuery because \"real time\" was said in a meeting. Ask what latency the decision actually needs."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Storage modes, composite models and Direct Lake docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20); DP-600 (2026-10-19)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Storage mode in Power BI Desktop","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/desktop-storage-mode"},{"title":"Use composite models","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/desktop-composite-models"},{"title":"Hybrid tables","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/service-dataset-modes-understand"}],"asg":[{"t":"DirectQuery reality check","time":"40 min","ds":"FactSalesBig in SQL (any free SQL: SQL Express, Postgres, or Fabric warehouse)","guidance":"A","steps":["Load FactSalesBig to a SQL database. Connect with DirectQuery. Import the dimensions.","Build the same summary page as Beginner. Open Performance Analyzer, copy a visual's DAX query and the generated SQL.","Add a measure with DISTINCTCOUNT and one with a text-based calculated column. Observe which one makes the SQL explode or fails (\"unsupported\").","Set \"Assume referential integrity\" on relationships and compare the SQL (INNER vs LEFT JOIN)."],"exp":"You can show one generated SQL statement before and after Assume referential integrity."},{"t":"Composite: extend a shared model","time":"40 min","ds":"Your published shared model","guidance":"A","steps":["Desktop → connect live to the published Northwind model. Then \"Make changes to this model\" to turn it into a DirectQuery-to-semantic-model composite.","Import a local Excel of sales targets and relate it to the remote DimRegion.","Note the \"limited relationship\" icon. Write a measure that uses both. Publish.","Delete a column in the source model and refresh the composite: read the error."],"exp":"A chain: your report → composite → shared model. You can explain what breaks upstream changes."},{"t":"Hybrid table","time":"30 min","ds":"FactSalesBig in SQL","guidance":"A","steps":["Incremental refresh policy on the DirectQuery table with \"Get the latest data in real time with DirectQuery\" on (needs Premium/Fabric capacity).","Publish, refresh, inspect partitions: import partitions for history and one DirectQuery partition for today.","Insert a row in SQL for today and confirm it appears without refresh."],"exp":"Today's data is live; history is imported."},{"t":"Storage mode decision table","time":"20 min","ds":"—","guidance":"A","steps":["Write a one-page decision table in a text box: for Import, DirectQuery, Dual, Direct Lake list max size, latency, DAX limitations, RLS behaviour, refresh needs.","Set DimProduct to Dual and explain in a comment why dimensions in a composite should be Dual."],"exp":"You choose Dual for dimensions shared between an import agg and a DQ fact, and you can say why."}],"int":[{"q":"Why should dimensions be in Dual storage mode in a composite model?","a":"Dual lets the engine answer from cache when the query only touches imported tables (the agg) and fall back to DirectQuery when joined to the DQ fact. Import-only dimensions would force a limited relationship to the DQ fact."},{"q":"What is a limited (weak) relationship?","a":"A relationship across source groups (e.g. import ↔ DirectQuery from different sources) or many-to-many. No blank row, RELATED does not work, referential integrity not assumed, filters pass as IN lists."},{"q":"DirectQuery over a shared semantic model: what is the security and refresh story?","a":"RLS on the source model applies; the composite can add its own RLS on local tables only. The remote part never refreshes locally; local import tables need their own schedule. Both models must live in workspaces the consumer can access or use \"Single sign-on\"-like chaining permissions."},{"q":"Give three DAX functions that are not supported or are slow over DirectQuery to SQL.","a":"Time intelligence over non-date columns, EARLIER-style iterators (turned into correlated subqueries), text functions in calculated columns, and DISTINCTCOUNT over large tables generating COUNT(DISTINCT) per group."},{"q":"When is Import the wrong choice even if the data fits?","a":"Regulatory need for real-time data, source of truth that changes every minute, data that must not leave the source system, or a model size that exceeds capacity memory once refreshed (needs 2× during refresh)."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"Assume referential integrity changes the generated SQL from:","o":["UNION to JOIN","LEFT OUTER JOIN to INNER JOIN","INNER to LEFT","No change"],"a":1,"why":"Inner joins are faster but hide fact rows with no matching dimension."},{"type":"mcq","q":"A Dual-mode table:","o":["Is always imported","Is always DirectQuery","Behaves as import or DQ depending on the query","Is a hybrid table"],"a":2,"why":"Dual is the definition of that behaviour."},{"type":"task","q":"Build a composite model over your shared Northwind model plus a local targets table, publish it, and list every feature that became unavailable versus a pure import model.","hint":"Calculated tables on remote, some format options, Q&A, certain visuals."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Hybrid tables require:","o":["Pro workspace","Premium/Fabric capacity","A gateway in personal mode","Dataflows"],"a":1,"why":"DirectQuery partitions within an incremental refresh policy are a capacity feature."}],"module":"advanced"},{"id":"a-deploy","name":"Deployment: pipelines, Git, PBIP, TMDL, XMLA, Tabular Editor","ds":["FactSales"],"skills":["deployment","testing"],"stage":"engineer","why":{"matters":"Without source control and promotion between environments, every change is made live in production and nobody can say what changed or roll it back.","failure":"Two developers overwrite each other's published model; a measure silently changes and the board pack is wrong for a week.","use":"PBIP + Git for every shared model; deployment pipelines or Fabric Git integration to move Dev → Test → Prod.","avoid":"Editing the production model directly through XMLA as a habit; it bypasses review and breaks .pbix download."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"PBIP overview and PBIR report format (Microsoft Learn, 2026-09-23); deployment pipelines docs","cert":"DP-600 (2026-10-19)","review_after_days":90},"refs":[{"title":"Power BI Desktop projects (PBIP)","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-overview"},{"title":"PBIR: project report folder","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-report"},{"title":"Deployment pipelines overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/intro-to-deployment-pipelines"},{"title":"Fabric Git integration","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/cicd/git-integration/intro-to-git-integration"}],"asg":[{"t":"PBIP and Git","time":"40 min","ds":"Your report","guidance":"A","steps":["Save your report as a Power BI Project: File → Save as → .pbip. Current Desktop builds save the model as TMDL and the report in PBIR, the enhanced report format that is now the default. Older builds needed preview switches for both.","Initialise a Git repo, commit. Open the folder: .SemanticModel/definition/*.tmdl and .Report/definition.","Change a measure in Desktop, save, git diff. Then change the same measure directly in the .tmdl file while the project is open: Desktop detects the external change and offers to apply it.","Connect the workspace to a Git branch (Fabric Git integration). Commit from Desktop, sync in the Service."],"exp":"A readable diff showing exactly one measure expression change."},{"t":"Deployment pipeline with rules","time":"40 min","ds":"Dev/Test/Prod workspaces","guidance":"A","steps":["Create a deployment pipeline with the three workspaces. Assign Dev.","Deploy to Test. Add a deployment rule that changes the Environment parameter (from the Intermediate parameter assignment) to \"Test\".","Compare Test vs Dev after changing a measure in Dev: the pipeline shows \"Different\". Deploy again.","Deploy only the semantic model, not the report, using selective deployment."],"exp":"Prod points at the Prod source without anyone editing the PBIX."},{"t":"Tabular Editor scripting","time":"40 min","ds":"Your model","guidance":"A","steps":["Open the model in Tabular Editor 2. Write a C# script that creates, for every measure ending in \"Sales\", a sibling measure \"{name} PY\" using SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR.","Run Best Practice Analyzer with the standard rules. Fix every violation, or document why not.","Use the XMLA endpoint (needs PPU/capacity) to open the published model, rename a measure, save. Note that the model can no longer be downloaded as PBIX.","Format all DAX with the built-in formatter."],"exp":"BPA shows 0 errors. You can list three BPA rules you disagree with and why."},{"t":"Semantic model versioning and rollback","time":"20 min","ds":"Your model","guidance":"A","steps":["Tag a Git commit as v1.0. Deploy. Make a breaking change (rename a column a report uses). Deploy.","Roll back by checking out the tag and syncing to the workspace.","Write a one-paragraph release note template you would send to report authors."],"exp":"The broken visual is fixed after the rollback without touching the report."}],"int":[{"q":"PBIX vs PBIP: why does it matter for a team?","a":"PBIX is a binary blob: no diffs, no merges, one person at a time. PBIP splits model (TMDL) and report (JSON) into text files that Git can diff and merge, and enables CI/CD and code review."},{"q":"What does a deployment rule change and what can it not change?","a":"Data source connections and parameter values per stage. It cannot change measures, RLS role membership or report content; those come from the deployed item."},{"q":"After editing a model via XMLA, why can't you download the PBIX anymore?","a":"The Service model has diverged from any PBIX; Desktop cannot round-trip arbitrary TOM changes. Your source of truth becomes the TMDL in Git."},{"q":"How do you deploy a model without triggering a full refresh?","a":"Deploy metadata only; the pipeline preserves data if the model structure allows. For incremental-refresh models, apply the refresh policy without data and refresh partitions in batches."},{"q":"What is the difference between Fabric Git integration and deployment pipelines, and do you use both?","a":"Git integration = source control and collaboration (branches, PRs). Pipelines = promotion between environments with rules. Typically Git for Dev, pipelines from Dev → Test → Prod, or Git-based deployment via API for full CI/CD."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"TMDL is:","o":["A DAX dialect","A text serialisation of the tabular model definition","A refresh log","A visual container"],"a":1,"why":"Tabular Model Definition Language: one file per table with measures, columns, relationships in plain text."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Deployment rules apply to:","o":["Reports","Semantic models and dataflows (parameters, sources)","Dashboards","Apps"],"a":1,"why":"Rules rewrite connection and parameter values on data items."},{"type":"task","q":"Save your model as PBIP, write a Tabular Editor script that adds a description to every measure lacking one, commit, and show the git diff line count.","hint":"foreach(var m in Model.AllMeasures) if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(m.Description)) m.Description = \"TODO\";"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Best Practice Analyzer rule \"Avoid bi-directional relationships\" fires. Best response:","o":["Always remove them","Justify or remove each; bridge-table security filters are a valid exception","Ignore BPA","Convert to many-to-many"],"a":1,"why":"Rules are guidance; document justified exceptions."}],"module":"advanced"},{"id":"a-fabric","name":"Dataflows, Fabric Lakehouse and Direct Lake","ds":["FactSales","FactInventory","WebEvents"],"skills":["fabric","modeling","performance"],"stage":"engineer","why":{"matters":"Storage mode decides how fresh the numbers are, how fast reports are and what the capacity costs. Choosing it wrongly is expensive to undo.","failure":"A Direct Lake on SQL model built over SQL views silently runs every query as DirectQuery, and the dashboard that was fast in the demo takes 20 seconds in production.","use":"Direct Lake when the data already lands in OneLake as Delta tables and is too large or too fresh to copy with Import.","avoid":"When the model author cannot change the upstream tables and needs Power Query transformations: use Import tables (possibly combined with Direct Lake on OneLake)."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"Direct Lake overview (Microsoft Learn, 2026-09-02) and How Direct Lake works (2026-09-09)","cert":"DP-600 (2026-10-19)","review_after_days":90},"refs":[{"title":"Direct Lake overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/fundamentals/direct-lake-overview"},{"title":"How Direct Lake works: framing, transcoding and fallback","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/fundamentals/direct-lake-how-it-works"},{"title":"Dataflow Gen2 overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/dataflows-gen2-overview"},{"title":"What is a lakehouse in Microsoft Fabric?","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/lakehouse-overview"}],"asg":[{"t":"Dataflow Gen2 as a shared staging layer","time":"40 min","ds":"RawOrdersExport","steps":["Create a Dataflow Gen2 in a Fabric workspace. Paste the RawOrdersExport clean-up M from Beginner.","Set the output destination to a Lakehouse table \"orders_clean\".","Point a new semantic model at the Lakehouse (SQL endpoint) and another at the Dataflow directly. Compare refresh behaviour.","Break the source (rename a column) and read the Dataflow error versus the model error."],"exp":"One transformation, two consumers, one place to fix it."},{"t":"Lakehouse and Direct Lake","time":"40 min","ds":"All datasets as CSV","steps":["Upload all fourteen CSVs to a Lakehouse Files area. Load each to a Delta table.","Create a Direct Lake semantic model from the Lakehouse and note which option you created: Direct Lake on OneLake (the recommended option for new models) or Direct Lake on SQL analytics endpoint. Build relationships in the web modeling view.","In DAX query view run EVALUATE TABLETRAITS() and read [DirectLakeFallbackInfo] for each table. None means the table is served by Direct Lake.","In the SQL analytics endpoint, create a view over FactSales and add it to a Direct Lake on SQL model. Run TABLETRAITS again: the view falls back to DirectQuery. Set the model's Direct Lake behavior to DirectLakeOnly and watch the same visual fail instead of falling back.","Try the same on a Direct Lake on OneLake model: it will not accept a non-materialized view at all. Materialize the logic as a Delta table instead."],"exp":"You can say what forces DirectQuery fallback in Direct Lake on SQL (SQL views, SQL-endpoint RLS, OLS or masking, guardrails exceeded, tables not yet framed) and why Direct Lake on OneLake never falls back: it errors instead, so you design to stay inside its limits."},{"t":"Notebook to Power BI","time":"40 min","ds":"WebEvents","steps":["In a Fabric notebook (PySpark or Python), load WebEvents, compute per-session first and last event and a funnel stage, write a Delta table \"sessions\".","Refresh the Direct Lake model (reframe) and build a funnel visual.","Schedule the notebook and the reframe in a pipeline."],"exp":"Funnel shows PageView → Purchase drop-off from the notebook output, not from DAX."},{"t":"Choose the right layer","time":"20 min","ds":"—","steps":["For each of these, write where the logic lives and why: currency conversion, customer ABC class, data cleaning of the messy export, budget allocation to days, RLS mapping, session duration.","Rule you are testing: transform as far upstream as possible, as far downstream as necessary."],"exp":"At most two of the six land in DAX."}],"int":[{"q":"Direct Lake vs Import vs DirectQuery.","a":"Import copies the data into VertiPaq at refresh time. DirectQuery sends every query to the source. Direct Lake loads Delta/Parquet columns from OneLake into VertiPaq on demand, so it is close to Import speed without copying data at refresh; \"refresh\" only reframes metadata. There are two Direct Lake options: Direct Lake on OneLake (recommended for new models, can combine several Fabric sources and Import tables, never falls back to DirectQuery) and Direct Lake on SQL analytics endpoint (one source, falls back to DirectQuery for SQL views, SQL-endpoint security or exceeded guardrails, controlled by the Direct Lake behavior property)."},{"q":"What is \"reframing\" in Direct Lake?","a":"Framing (\"reframing\") makes the model point at the latest version of each Delta table by reading the Delta log. No data is copied, and only changed column segments are reloaded on the next query. It runs automatically when \"Keep your Direct Lake data up to date\" is on, or on demand, on a schedule or through the API when you need ETL to finish before users see new data."},{"q":"When does a Dataflow beat Power Query inside the model?","a":"When multiple models need the same transformed table, when the transformation is heavy and should run once, when you want a lakehouse table other tools can read, or when the source needs a gateway that only the dataflow should touch."},{"q":"Where should a business rule like \"returns are excluded from revenue\" live?","a":"As upstream as possible in a shared table (Lakehouse view or dataflow) so every tool agrees, then exposed as a documented measure in a certified model. Never in individual reports."},{"q":"What is the SQL analytics endpoint and what is it not for?","a":"A read-only T-SQL surface over Lakehouse Delta tables. Good for ad-hoc queries and views; not for writes and not the preferred path for Power BI when Direct Lake is available."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"A Direct Lake on SQL analytics endpoint model falls back to DirectQuery when:","o":["The model has more than 4 tables","A table is based on a non-materialized SQL view, or the SQL endpoint applies RLS/OLS","It is refreshed (framed)","The semantic model itself has RLS roles"],"a":1,"why":"SQL views and SQL-endpoint security force DirectQuery fallback in Direct Lake on SQL. Semantic-model RLS does not. Direct Lake on OneLake never falls back: those cases error instead."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Dataflow Gen2 output destination options include:","o":["Only the dataflow storage","Lakehouse, Warehouse, KQL DB, Azure SQL among others","Only OneDrive","Only Excel"],"a":1,"why":"Gen2 can write to multiple Fabric and Azure destinations."},{"type":"task","q":"Build a Direct Lake model over the 14 CSVs and reproduce the Beginner executive page. Prove one visual is served by Direct Lake, not fallback.","hint":"Run EVALUATE TABLETRAITS() and check [DirectLakeFallbackInfo] = None for every table, or look for DirectQuery events in a DAX Studio trace."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Reframing a Direct Lake model:","o":["Copies all data again","Re-reads Delta metadata only","Requires a gateway","Deletes the cache permanently"],"a":1,"why":"Framing is a metadata operation: it points the model at the latest Delta files. Columns load into memory on first query (transcoding)."}],"module":"advanced"},{"id":"a-gov","name":"Governance, enterprise architecture and the \"senior\" conversations","ds":["FactSales","DimEmployee"],"skills":["governance","security","communication"],"stage":"architect","why":{"matters":"Governance is what lets a company trust a number without asking who built it.","failure":"Three \"Revenue\" reports disagree in a board meeting and nobody knows which model is authoritative.","use":"Certification for models that many reports depend on, sensitivity labels for anything confidential, usage and lineage to decide what to retire.","avoid":"Governance as a gate that blocks every change. Make the certified path the easiest path."},"verified":{"date":"2026-10-01","context":"OLS, endorsement, usage metrics and lineage docs, Sept 2026","cert":"PL-300 (2026-04-20); DP-600 (2026-10-19)","review_after_days":120},"refs":[{"title":"Object-level security","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/security/service-admin-object-level-security"},{"title":"Endorsement overview","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/endorsement-overview"},{"title":"Lineage view","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/lineage"}],"asg":[{"t":"Object-level security","time":"20 min","ds":"DimEmployee","guidance":"A","steps":["In Tabular Editor, create a role \"NoSalary\" and set OLS on DimEmployee[Salary] to None.","Publish. Add a test user. Open the report: the visual using Salary must show an error, others must work.","Combine with the RLS role and confirm both apply."],"exp":"Only the salary visual breaks for the restricted user; you can explain why OLS breaks the visual instead of hiding the column."},{"t":"Certified model with documentation","time":"30 min","ds":"Your shared model","guidance":"A","steps":["Add descriptions to every visible measure and table (Tabular Editor script from the Deployment topic).","Add synonyms for Q&A on the top five fields.","Request certification from your admin (or certify as admin in a trial tenant). Add a sensitivity label.","Create a \"Model guide\" report page listing every measure, its definition and owner, generated from INFO.MEASURES() in a DAX query."],"exp":"Analysts can find and understand the model without asking you."},{"t":"Usage and lineage","time":"20 min","ds":"Your workspace","guidance":"A","steps":["Open the usage metrics report for your report. Find the least-viewed page.","Open lineage view for the workspace. Identify everything that breaks if the Lakehouse is deleted.","Use the Admin monitoring workspace (or the Fabric Capacity Metrics app) to find the model consuming the most CU."],"exp":"A list of three items you would retire and one you would optimise."},{"t":"The senior conversation","time":"30 min","ds":"—","guidance":"A","steps":["Write, in under 200 words each, your answer to: (1) \"Why is the report slow?\" for a CFO, (2) the same for a data engineer. (3) \"Should we go Fabric?\" for a CTO. (4) \"Why can't I just export everything to Excel?\" for an analyst.","Read them aloud. Cut any sentence a listener would not understand."],"exp":"Four answers, none containing the word VertiPaq for the CFO, all containing a recommendation."}],"int":[{"q":"Design a semantic-model architecture for 50 reports across 6 departments.","a":"One certified enterprise model per domain (Sales, Finance, HR) with conformed date/customer/product dimensions, owned by a central team, living in models-only workspaces. Departmental workspaces hold reports live-connected or composite-extended. Dev/Test/Prod via pipelines, Git for models, BPA in CI. Self-service models allowed only in personal or sandbox workspaces and never certified."},{"q":"OLS vs RLS vs hiding a column.","a":"Hiding is cosmetic (Analyze in Excel still shows it). RLS filters rows. OLS removes the column/table from the metadata for the role; any visual referencing it errors, so build separate reports per audience."},{"q":"What are the key tenant settings you review on day one at a new company?","a":"Export to Excel/CSV, publish to web, external sharing, who can create workspaces, who can certify, Fabric enablement, sensitivity label enforcement, XMLA read/write, and the usage metrics setting."},{"q":"How do you handle a request for a report you know is wrong (e.g. summing a snapshot)?","a":"Show the requester the wrong number and the right one on the same page with the definition of each, agree the definition in writing, put it in the certified model, and reference it in the report. Refusing helps nobody; educating does."},{"q":"What is your checklist before calling a model production-ready?","a":"Star schema, marked date table, no unused columns, integer keys, measures documented, BPA clean, RLS tested with View as and a real user, refresh tested from the Service with the gateway, performance under 2 seconds per visual on the expected data volume, ownership and support path documented, sensitivity label applied."},{"q":"How do you estimate capacity needs?","a":"Measure the model size after optimisation and 2× it for refresh, count concurrent users from usage metrics, run a load test, look at the Capacity Metrics app for CU per interactive query and per refresh, and leave 30% headroom."}],"ass":[{"type":"mcq","q":"A user in an OLS role opens a visual using a restricted column. Result:","o":["Column hidden, visual works","Visual shows an error","Blank values","The role is ignored"],"a":1,"why":"OLS removes the object from the metadata; references to it fail."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Certification of a semantic model can be granted by:","o":["Any Pro user","Users/groups allowed by the tenant setting","Workspace Viewers","Only Microsoft"],"a":1,"why":"Certification is governed by a tenant setting listing who may certify."},{"type":"task","q":"Produce the \"Model guide\" page using INFO.MEASURES() and INFO.TABLES() in a DAX query, exported to a table in a report, and include the description column.","hint":"EVALUATE SELECTCOLUMNS(INFO.MEASURES(), \"Measure\", [Name], \"Expression\", [Expression], \"Description\", [Description])."},{"type":"mcq","q":"Lineage view helps you answer:","o":["Which measure is slow","Which downstream items depend on a source","Who viewed a report","How much a capacity costs"],"a":1,"why":"Lineage shows dependency chains between sources, dataflows, models and reports."}],"module":"advanced"}]}
];
